cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it, and cite the reference DNS dataset below."
title: "ML-Augmented RANS Modelling of Separated Flow Using DNS Reference Data"
authors:
  - family-names: Bainbridge
    given-names: Thomas
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ThomasBainbridge/ml-augmented-rans-separated-flow"
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - turbulence modelling
  - RANS
  - machine learning
  - data-driven closure
  - periodic hills
  - OpenFOAM
abstract: >
  A reproducible study of whether a lightweight, interpretable machine-learning
  correction can reduce RANS (k-omega SST) model-form error for separated flow
  over periodic hills, validated against DNS across five hill geometries. The
  project spans an a-priori eddy-viscosity correction, a coupled custom-solver
  a-posteriori test, a tensor-basis neural network, nonlocal features, and a
  Reynolds-stress anisotropy correction, and maps where — and why — data-driven
  closure helps and where it does not.
